  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Bento vivo",
    "overview": "The corporate site is a board of working cells, not an agency landing page. A visitor uses a slice of each product before reading a claim: a DypOS kitchen ticket moves across columns, a moyiq expense typed in plain words is categorised and subtracted, an Esmalia appointment gets confirmed over WhatsApp. All three run on sample data and say so. Around them, the company proves it operates: status pills measured by `/api/status`, a dated log, the Florida registry strip.\n\nThe ground is a cool, quiet grey with white cells; the whole board is light and calm so the products can be loud. Maxnova itself speaks in one colour, an electric cobalt that never decorates: it takes over entire fields (the AI service cell, the first log stat, the closing footer band with its poster-scale claim) or marks the one primary action. Product colours are guests: each one appears only inside its own product's cell, demo, tag or page section, and a product cell floods with its brand colour on hover or focus.\n\nDepth is flat. Cells are separated by a 16px gap and a hairline, not by shadows. The only motion is functional: the demos animate the step a user just took, status dots pulse when a measurement lands, the \"Check again\" icon spins while re-measuring. `prefers-reduced-motion` turns all of it off.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "12-column bento of white 16px-radius cells on a cool grey ground.",
      "One electric cobalt that owns whole fields, never sprinkled.",
      "Product cells take their own brand colour on hover; guest colours stay inside their product.",
      "Live, honest signals: grey until measured, green only after a real answer.",
      "Bricolage Grotesque display at optical size 96, Schibsted Grotesk for everything readable.",
      "Light theme only."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Whole Field Rule",
        "body": "Cobalt either owns an entire surface (a cell, a stat, the footer band) or marks a single action or link. It is never a thin decorative accent, gradient or glow.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Guest Colour Rule",
        "body": "A product colour may appear only where that product is the subject. Outside its own cell or section, a product is named in ink or represented by its own logo.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Measured Green Rule",
        "body": "Green is a fact, not a colour choice. Nothing turns green until a real measurement says so.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Ochre Rule",
        "body": "Maxnova's colours are vivid and high-impact. It never uses ochre, bronze or dull gold. When a vivid colour cannot carry white text at contrast, the text goes in ink on the full colour (DypOS orange takes dark text), the colour is never dulled.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Only Where Numbers Line Up Rule",
        "body": "Tabular figures are switched on only for clocks, latency, demo counters and log stats. Schibsted's tabular set widens punctuation, so prose and prices keep proportional figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Eyebrow Rule",
        "body": "No small label, kicker or eyebrow sits above a heading. A heading opens its block.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Board Rule",
        "body": "Cells never carry a resting shadow. If a cell needs emphasis, it changes field (white to cobalt, ink or tint), not elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep cells white on the `ground`, 16px radius, 16px gap, hairline border, no resting shadow.",
      "**Do** let cobalt own a whole field or a single action; use `cobalt-tint` with `cobalt-ink` for the quiet variant.",
      "**Do** keep product colours, logos and demos inside their own product cell or section.",
      "**Do** show a status as grey \"No data\" until a real measurement returns, then green or red.",
      "**Do** label every demo and screenshot honestly (sample data, real demo screen or public page, capture date).",
      "**Do** use pills for every control and tabular figures only for clocks, latency and counters.",
      "**Do** keep vivid colours vivid: put ink text on a colour that cannot carry white."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** invent customers, numbers or testimonials; the site says plainly that the company is early.",
      "**Don't** put a kicker or eyebrow above a heading.",
      "**Don't** recolour a product or borrow a product's colour for Maxnova surfaces.",
      "**Don't** use ochre, bronze or dull gold anywhere.",
      "**Don't** add a dark theme; the site is light only.",
      "**Don't** use gradient text, glass cards or glow; the sticky nav's blur is the only translucency.",
      "**Don't** introduce a third typeface or a mono face."
    ]
  }
}